OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Wed 12 Aug to Fri 21 AugFA
OL,6,Fmixed start is likely to this period,
OL,7,Fwith some rain or showers in the north
OL,8,Fand quite breezy conditions while in
OL,9,Fthe south it will be mostly dry, sunny
OL,10,Fand hot, even very hot in some places.
OL,11,FSouthern parts are likely to turn
OL,12,Fcooler and fresher next weekend
OL,13,Fthough. Further into August, areas of
OL,14,Flow pressure may start to track
OL,15,Ffurther south and east. This means
OL,16,Fthere is a greater chance of frontal
OL,17,Fsystems or thundery interludes
OL,18,Faffecting southern and eastern areas
OL,19,Fin comparison to recent weeks, though
OL,20,Frainfall amounts could be quite
OL,21,Fvariable with some areas still seeing
OL,22,Frelatively little. Temperatures are
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Flikely to remain above average,
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fespecially in the south, where it may
OL,25,Fbe very warm or hot at times.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
